From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:22:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tools/libcompat: gather <elf.h> itself

`head/link.h` includes <elf.h>, meaning illumos' own. Without it in the
gathered set the include falls through to glibc's, whose Elf32_Dyn,
Elf32_Syminfo and friends then conflict with the ones <sys/link.h> just
declared.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 usr/src/tools/libcompat/Makefile | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/tools/libcompat/Makefile b/usr/src/tools/libcompat/Makefile
index f949d585f6..c173b9259a 100644
--- a/usr/src/tools/libcompat/Makefile
+++ b/usr/src/tools/libcompat/Makefile
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ MACHSYSHDRS=	sys/machtypes.h
 # and <sys/auxv_SPARC.h> beside it, and nothing in the list says so; staging
 # auxv.h alone is a known way to break elfextract.  They move together.
 #
-HEADHDRS=	dlfcn.h \
+HEADHDRS=	elf.h \
+		dlfcn.h \
 		gelf.h \
 		libelf.h \
 		proc_service.h \
